      "text": "We start with the given expression \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and expand it step by step.\n\nFirst, we use the distributive property to expand the product:\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x).\n\\]\nNext, we perform the multiplications:\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot 7 = 21x^2,\n\\]\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) = -6x^3,\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x \\cdot 7 = -35x,\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x \\cdot (-2x) = 10x^2,\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 7 = 28,\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot (-2x) = -8x.\n\\]\nNow, we combine all these terms:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 21x^2 + 10x^2 - 35x - 8x + 28.\n\\]\nWe combine the like terms:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28 = -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28.\n\\]\nThus, the expression \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) can be written in the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\) where \\(a = -6\\), \\(b = 31\\), \\(c = -43\\), and \\(d = 28\\).\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28.\n\\]\nWe compute each term:\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48,\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124,\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86,\n\\]\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28 = 18.\n\\]\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}.\n\\]",
