      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to expand the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and then identify the coefficients \\(a, b, c,\\) and \\(d\\) of the polynomial \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\). The goal is to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\).\n\nFirst, let's expand \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\):\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) - 5x \\cdot 7 - 5x \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate each term:\n\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot 7 = 21x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) = -6x^3\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x \\cdot 7 = -35x\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x \\cdot (-2x) = 10x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 7 = 28\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot (-2x) = -8x\n\\]\n\nNow, let's combine all these terms:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 21x^2 + 10x^2 - 35x - 8x + 28\n\\]\n\nCombine the like terms:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nFrom this, we can identify the coefficients \\(a, b, c,\\) and \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\\[\n= -48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\\[\n= 28\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{28}\n\\]",
